Lobium - coherent one-time canvas and ImageBitmap readback farbling.

Split out of core/config-channel.patch so the canvas surface owns its own hooks.

The shared kernel is lobium::FarbleCanvasRgba (//components/lobium_fp/lobium_farble.cc, an added
file, not part of this patch). It nudges R/G/B by {-1,0,+1} keyed on (seed, ABSOLUTE canvas
coordinate, channel), and only for pixels that are byte-identical to none of their four orthogonal
neighbours. Solid fills, hard edges between fills, and cleared canvases therefore read back exactly,
while anti-aliased and blended pixels (where cross-host entropy lives) are projected. Absolute
coordinates keep full-canvas and sub-rectangle reads coherent.

Readback hooks:
  1. BaseRenderingContext2D::getImageData farbles the newly allocated private ImageData buffer.
  2. HTMLCanvasElement::toDataURL/toBlob farble a private unpremultiplied snapshot.
  3. OffscreenCanvas::convertToBlob covers the worker-only encode path.
The seed is seeds.canvas for 2D and bitmaprenderer output, and seeds.webgl for WebGL. All paths are
no-ops when their seed is zero. getImageData projects unorm8, float16, and float32 from one canonical
RGBA8888 apron. Only kernel-selected, finite [0,1] float RGB channels are converted through Skia to
q/255; untouched channels, alpha, and extended-range/non-finite values retain their native bits.
Encode paths still leave non-8888 backing canvases unchanged rather than truncating.

Farbling is one-time. Canvas draw provenance distinguishes known page pixels from host-rasterized
pixels: solid writes and decoded raster images stay exact; text, paths, SVG, gradients, filters,
shadows, video, WebGL, and unknown producers remain fail-safe entropy-bearing. The provenance bit is
preserved across ImageData construction, ImageBitmap crop/copy, HTML/Offscreen canvas construction,
decoded image factories, transient structured clone and worker transfer, OffscreenCanvas 2D
transferToImageBitmap, bitmaprenderer transferFrom/transferTo, and exported worker frames backing a
transferControlToOffscreen HTML placeholder. Direct drawImage from decoded raster images and
known-pixel canvases preserves it as well.

The bit defaults to true. Old or unclassified paths therefore keep farbling rather than opening a
pristine-pixel bypass. Persistent structured-clone wire-format-v21 records are deliberately not
extended: older IndexedDB records and downgrade reads default true, while transient same-build clone
and transfer messages carry the exact bit.



